    "signature": "fn get_coerce_type_for_list(expr_type: &arrow::datatypes::DataType, list_types: &[arrow::datatypes::DataType]) -> Option<arrow::datatypes::DataType>",
    "docs": "Attempts to coerce the types of `list_types` to be comparable with the\n`expr_type` for IN list predicates.\nReturns the common data type for `expr_type` and `list_types`.\n\nUses comparison coercion because `x IN (a, b)` is semantically equivalent\nto `x = a OR x = b`.",
